WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:10.930
NAN BODEN: Good afternoon.

00:00:10.930 --> 00:00:12.980
I'm delighted to be here today.

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:14.620
I know you've heard
a lot about what

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:17.380
we're doing in Google
Cloud on the sale's side,

00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:19.480
on the product's side,
and some about our go

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:21.090
to market channels.

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:22.730
I'm really excited
to talk to you today

00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:24.229
about what we've
been doing and what

00:00:24.229 --> 00:00:27.290
we're in the process of really
building in our Tech Partner's

00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:28.900
organization.

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:31.280
This organization came
together just a few months ago

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:33.860
to really focus on our
Tech Partners ecosystem.

00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:38.000
And by that, we mean independent
software vendors and also

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:40.000
our top strategic partners.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.770
We've been scaling
this operation.

00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:44.040
In fact as Diane
mentioned earlier,

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:46.840
sometimes the rate of the
scaling is kind of dizzying.

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:48.420
But I want you to
understand what

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:49.650
our philosophy is for that.

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:51.780
And so, hopefully, we
can partner with you

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:54.540
and many of your
customers about how

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:58.110
we take this ecosystem forward.

00:00:58.110 --> 00:00:59.580
So when we first
started thinking

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:01.427
about what it means
to partner, we

00:01:01.427 --> 00:01:03.010
started thinking
about our principles.

00:01:03.010 --> 00:01:05.007
And I want to run
you through those.

00:01:05.007 --> 00:01:07.340
But then, I want to tell you
how we operationalize them.

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:09.450
And how I think that's
really quite different.

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:11.616
And how it's going to make
an even bigger difference

00:01:11.616 --> 00:01:13.560
in what we build together.

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:15.790
First of all, we want
to be the open platform

00:01:15.790 --> 00:01:16.912
and the open partner.

00:01:16.912 --> 00:01:19.370
And you've heard that a lot
from Brian Stevens this morning

00:01:19.370 --> 00:01:21.100
about how open we
are with respect

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:22.820
to things like open source.

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:25.600
But in this case, the openness
extends even further than that.

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:27.680
And I'll talk about
a couple of examples

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:29.910
where that openness
really changes the way

00:01:29.910 --> 00:01:32.161
our partnering is put together.

00:01:32.161 --> 00:01:34.410
We also want to bring more
innovation than just Google

00:01:34.410 --> 00:01:35.327
could bring by itself.

00:01:35.327 --> 00:01:36.784
And that's really
one of the tenets

00:01:36.784 --> 00:01:38.990
that Diane laid out early
on about our partnering--

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:42.210
is that we really want to
have a much bigger innovation

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:46.120
story than any one company,
even a company of Google size

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:46.620
could build.

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:48.290
And building that
with our partners

00:01:48.290 --> 00:01:50.810
is something that really
excites our engineers.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:53.150
And particularly as we take
it into new applications

00:01:53.150 --> 00:01:54.460
and new markets.

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:56.170
You know, fairness
and transparency

00:01:56.170 --> 00:01:58.160
are really core
tenants of Google.

00:01:58.160 --> 00:01:59.920
And that fairness
and transparency

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:01.540
when extended to
partners, I think

00:02:01.540 --> 00:02:03.890
gives us a real strong
competitive advantage

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:06.020
in that people want to
partner with Google,

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:08.259
because we're going to
be fair and transparent

00:02:08.259 --> 00:02:11.340
and bring innovation
to a bigger market.

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:13.990
And all of that results
in a shared success.

00:02:13.990 --> 00:02:17.660
And Diana said it very often,
that our success is really

00:02:17.660 --> 00:02:18.680
our partner's success.

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:20.650
If our partners
are not successful,

00:02:20.650 --> 00:02:23.560
you know, then it's really
just academic what we're doing.

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:25.610
And so, we've really
been focusing a lot

00:02:25.610 --> 00:02:28.120
on, not just the technical
and the integration

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:29.870
parts of how we work
with our partners,

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:31.640
but what are the
business models?

00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:33.700
How do we make sure
that they're successful?

00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:35.440
How do we split
that value that we

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:38.030
create in the world in a
fair and appropriate way,

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:41.340
so that we can sustain
more and more of this?

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:43.922
So some of this I know seems
kind of uncontroversial,

00:02:43.922 --> 00:02:45.630
like who would vote
against these things?

00:02:45.630 --> 00:02:47.950
But when we really start
to operationalize it,

00:02:47.950 --> 00:02:50.580
some really cool things happen.

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:52.660
We looked very early on
at some of the thinking

00:02:52.660 --> 00:02:55.340
that-- very typical
stuff that goes on.

00:02:55.340 --> 00:02:57.880
Let's say, we've got a new
idea out there in the world,

00:02:57.880 --> 00:03:00.060
should I build or
should I partner?

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:02.490
And that build or
partner can really

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:04.130
be a kind of long
and painful thought.

00:03:04.130 --> 00:03:05.130
You know, like should I?

00:03:05.130 --> 00:03:05.520
I don't know.

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:07.520
Maybe I should build,
maybe I should partner.

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:09.430
And what we decided was
this is really the wrong way

00:03:09.430 --> 00:03:10.179
to think about it.

00:03:10.179 --> 00:03:13.050
If you're really the open
partner and the open platform,

00:03:13.050 --> 00:03:15.930
you should do both or you
should be open to doing both.

00:03:15.930 --> 00:03:18.010
That we should
build and partner.

00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:21.410
And that's been a really
liberating concept for us,

00:03:21.410 --> 00:03:23.900
not just in terms of what
we're able to do with partners,

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:26.101
but also our internal
product teams.

00:03:26.101 --> 00:03:27.600
You know, they
understand they don't

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:29.933
have to build every single
feature everybody thought of.

00:03:29.933 --> 00:03:32.030
We can wind up
doing things where

00:03:32.030 --> 00:03:35.090
we cover much more of the
innovation and market space

00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:36.350
by doing both.

00:03:36.350 --> 00:03:39.060
So recently, we've had two
really exciting examples

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:40.780
of that.

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:43.350
You've heard of some this
morning from Evernote

00:03:43.350 --> 00:03:45.580
and also a deal we
just had with Box.

00:03:45.580 --> 00:03:49.420
These are very clear examples
of the strategy where Google

00:03:49.420 --> 00:03:51.180
has products in each
of these spaces,

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:53.180
but there's a very
big world out there

00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:55.320
and a huge, huge
number of customers

00:03:55.320 --> 00:03:58.600
who prefer Box and who prefer
Evernote for their needs.

00:03:58.600 --> 00:04:02.670
And when we partner together, we
create a much bigger ecosystem.

00:04:02.670 --> 00:04:04.310
And so, each of
them has been using

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:06.000
different points
of what Google has

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:10.190
to offer in terms of products
and technology, from G Suite

00:04:10.190 --> 00:04:13.090
to Cloud to Springboard
search and assist

00:04:13.090 --> 00:04:15.380
and also all of our machine
learning techniques.

00:04:15.380 --> 00:04:19.050
And so, if you think about
this model for how even though

00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:20.860
Google may now or
may in the future

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:22.790
have a product in
a certain space,

00:04:22.790 --> 00:04:26.650
it's still a wide open field for
how we can innovate together.

00:04:26.650 --> 00:04:28.880
Just as exciting
for that is how, not

00:04:28.880 --> 00:04:31.330
just the things in Google
Cloud that we bring,

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:34.220
but if you think about the
entire portfolio of what Google

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:36.910
has to offer in products
and technologies.

00:04:36.910 --> 00:04:38.710
One of the best
things that I've found

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:40.610
in the sort of three
short months we've

00:04:40.610 --> 00:04:44.720
been doing this new
organization for Tech Partners,

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:47.540
has been that our friends
in other parts of Google,

00:04:47.540 --> 00:04:51.200
like in AdWords and Analytics,
and Play, and YouTube-- I mean,

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:53.480
they're super excited
about us being

00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:55.640
able to partner
with other companies

00:04:55.640 --> 00:04:57.420
to really bring what
is the power of one

00:04:57.420 --> 00:04:59.060
Google to those markets.

00:04:59.060 --> 00:05:02.765
And really to innovate in not
just technology, but in the way

00:05:02.765 --> 00:05:04.160
the business is put together.

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:05.910
To transform industries.

00:05:05.910 --> 00:05:08.890
And that's something that
my organization is just

00:05:08.890 --> 00:05:11.040
on fire with how
exciting it is to be

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:14.140
able to work on these
things with our partners.

00:05:14.140 --> 00:05:16.060
I'm blessed with a
great number of members

00:05:16.060 --> 00:05:19.180
of my team, who are both
engineers, and MBAs,

00:05:19.180 --> 00:05:21.840
and business people,
and BD folks.

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:23.280
And just putting
that all together

00:05:23.280 --> 00:05:26.920
in a way that basically
moves the needle forward.

00:05:26.920 --> 00:05:28.780
Certainly for us and
for our partners,

00:05:28.780 --> 00:05:31.240
it's just been
tremendously exciting.

00:05:31.240 --> 00:05:35.290
We look at a different ISVs by
a bunch of different sectors.

00:05:35.290 --> 00:05:37.100
And so, there's
all kinds of ways

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:39.980
to intergage with Google
about our organization,

00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:41.750
about how you go
about partnering.

00:05:41.750 --> 00:05:44.750
And so, we have experts
in each of these areas.

00:05:44.750 --> 00:05:46.760
If you're in data and
analytics in the Cloud

00:05:46.760 --> 00:05:49.060
or if you're in
visualization, we

00:05:49.060 --> 00:05:51.340
have a lot of different
programs for each of those.

00:05:51.340 --> 00:05:53.920
And so, it's been a
really exciting time

00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:56.530
to put that together and
start to really take that out

00:05:56.530 --> 00:05:57.030
to market.

00:05:57.030 --> 00:05:59.321
And you're starting to see
deals that we're announcing.

00:05:59.321 --> 00:06:01.742
And of course, we're
working on a lot more.

00:06:01.742 --> 00:06:03.200
The other thing
that we're doing is

00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:04.741
we're investing in
the infrastructure

00:06:04.741 --> 00:06:05.550
for our partners.

00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:07.530
And the acquisition
that we did recently

00:06:07.530 --> 00:06:11.350
of Orbitera, which is an
e-commerce Cloud platform,

00:06:11.350 --> 00:06:13.070
multi-cloud back end.

00:06:13.070 --> 00:06:15.850
They provide really
nice test drives

00:06:15.850 --> 00:06:18.500
and one of the more
elegant billing systems

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:21.560
that I've seen certainly on
the cloud platforms-- you know,

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:24.360
for being able to handle
all the major public clouds.

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:27.990
I mean, the Orbitera
platform allows our ISVs

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:29.230
to plug into that.

00:06:29.230 --> 00:06:31.610
And then, it really
simplifies their ability

00:06:31.610 --> 00:06:34.490
to deploy and have
their customers use

00:06:34.490 --> 00:06:35.260
any of the clouds.

00:06:35.260 --> 00:06:37.000
And this is something
that we want

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:38.660
to lower that friction
for our partner,

00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:42.470
so especially the ISVs can
get to market faster, and be

00:06:42.470 --> 00:06:45.190
able to deliver their
services, and grow

00:06:45.190 --> 00:06:46.685
their businesses better.

00:06:46.685 --> 00:06:48.310
The other thing you
heard earlier today

00:06:48.310 --> 00:06:50.159
was the acquisition of Apigee.

00:06:50.159 --> 00:06:51.700
One of the things
that I really enjoy

00:06:51.700 --> 00:06:53.380
about thinking through
how this is going

00:06:53.380 --> 00:06:55.460
to affect our partners--
is that, if you

00:06:55.460 --> 00:06:57.942
use one of Apigee's,
I think, really

00:06:57.942 --> 00:07:00.400
illustrative examples of one
of their customers, Walgreens,

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:02.760
you can see how this
kind of framework

00:07:02.760 --> 00:07:06.580
can help us move partnering and
the integration of applications

00:07:06.580 --> 00:07:08.060
forward much faster.

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:09.940
This example shows
Walgreens that

00:07:09.940 --> 00:07:12.750
may have started with the
idea of, oh, hey look.

00:07:12.750 --> 00:07:15.925
I can do a photo prints
API, wouldn't that be great?

00:07:15.925 --> 00:07:17.300
You know, because
now we can just

00:07:17.300 --> 00:07:20.280
print photos with an API call.

00:07:20.280 --> 00:07:21.990
And over time, they
grew to say, well,

00:07:21.990 --> 00:07:25.480
you know not only do I
need to print photos and be

00:07:25.480 --> 00:07:27.730
able to do just
that with an API,

00:07:27.730 --> 00:07:29.130
what about my prescriptions?

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:31.570
You know, I can have
folks be able to refill

00:07:31.570 --> 00:07:33.410
their prescriptions
with an API and I can

00:07:33.410 --> 00:07:35.250
do my rewards program that way.

00:07:35.250 --> 00:07:37.380
And before you know
it, especially when

00:07:37.380 --> 00:07:39.100
they announced this
to the outside world,

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:42.410
all of a sudden you have
Imager and Instagram

00:07:42.410 --> 00:07:43.490
trying to print photos.

00:07:43.490 --> 00:07:47.630
And you have WebMD hooked up
to their prescription's APIs.

00:07:47.630 --> 00:07:50.030
And that framework for
being able to integrate now

00:07:50.030 --> 00:07:53.370
hundreds of APIs
quickly and securely

00:07:53.370 --> 00:07:56.030
and be able to make sure that
there's not any kind of falling

00:07:56.030 --> 00:07:58.190
over as you try
to scale, is what

00:07:58.190 --> 00:08:01.140
I think allows us to have a
framework that our partners can

00:08:01.140 --> 00:08:04.500
really build some exciting
applications-- in a way that

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:06.540
really gets them
to market quickly

00:08:06.540 --> 00:08:08.040
and allows us to
put things together

00:08:08.040 --> 00:08:10.200
that might have been too
hard to do in other ways.

00:08:10.200 --> 00:08:13.190
So I'm very excited about
both of these acquisitions,

00:08:13.190 --> 00:08:14.800
because they allow
our partners to be

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:16.556
a lot more successful quicker.

00:08:16.556 --> 00:08:17.930
And that's the
thing that we want

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:20.430
to use going forward as we
try to build even deeper tech

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:22.050
partnerships.

00:08:22.050 --> 00:08:23.820
So the message of
the story today

00:08:23.820 --> 00:08:27.250
is that we've really been taking
a different view to partnering

00:08:27.250 --> 00:08:30.220
certainly than Google's had
available in and around Cloud.

00:08:30.220 --> 00:08:32.470
We took several groups
and put them together

00:08:32.470 --> 00:08:35.070
in terms of groups that were
already doing some partnering.

00:08:35.070 --> 00:08:37.679
Gave them a much bigger
scope, a much bigger mission.

00:08:37.679 --> 00:08:39.380
And tripled the
size of the group.

00:08:39.380 --> 00:08:41.460
And we are really on
fire with how well we

00:08:41.460 --> 00:08:43.967
want to go about doing things
that really make a difference.

00:08:43.967 --> 00:08:46.050
And so, if you think about
partnering with Google,

00:08:46.050 --> 00:08:47.758
particularly on the
tech partnering side,

00:08:47.758 --> 00:08:50.550
I can tell you for sure, now is
the time that you should really

00:08:50.550 --> 00:08:52.820
be doing that
investigation with us.

00:08:52.820 --> 00:08:54.400
Because it just
seems like there's

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:57.110
so many things to be
going at here in terms

00:08:57.110 --> 00:08:59.870
of really bringing
innovation to our customers

00:08:59.870 --> 00:09:01.410
and really transforming
industries.

00:09:01.410 --> 00:09:03.810
So we are open for business
and we would certainly

00:09:03.810 --> 00:09:06.862
love to talk to folks about
how to do more tech partnering.

00:09:06.862 --> 00:09:08.070
Thank you for your attention.

00:09:08.070 --> 00:09:10.620
[APPLAUSE]

